Z||000002||PBJ||05-23-2001||09:06 PM||||To replace a heater core in a fiero is a simple chore.  Not much longer than rigging up some by pass.  You access it from under the frt hood behind were the hoses go in.||||reg||1
Z||000003||cadaver||05-23-2001||11:08 PM||||Two hoses and four screws. Thats it in an A/C car. I think the non a/c cars are a little different.<BR>You disconnect the hoses from under the hood. And the screws and cover from under the pass. side dash. Oh and you need to remove the little bracket with the door chime thing on it. And the sub box if equiped. To fill just remove both caps. One from the radiator and one from the thermostat housing. Fill till it comes out the radiator. Then cap. Then fill some more. Once full crack the rad. cap till the bubbles quit. Then fill some more. And reinstall the thermostat. That should be it.<BR>I installed a flip vent cap on my radiator to make things easier. Thats when I used to work on the system alot. Havent touched it for two years now.||||reg||1
